    "A 14-year-old was taken into custody by Delhi police for allegedly hacking a test portal.",
    "The youth is accused of stealing sensitive recruitment data related to the Agniveer program.",
    "Authorities identified efforts by the teenager to offer the stolen information for sale on the dark web."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Delhi police have apprehended a 14-year-old suspect following reports of a significant cybersecurity breach. The teenager is accused of infiltrating a testing platform to extract information related to the Agniveer recruitment scheme. According to investigators, the suspect subsequently attempted to monetize the stolen data by placing it for sale on the dark web. The Agniveer program is a recruitment scheme for the Indian armed forces. This incident, reported by multiple outlets, highlights ongoing concerns regarding the security of digital platforms used for government-led recruitment processes. Law enforcement officials confirmed the arrest as part of their response to the illicit distribution of sensitive information online. Further investigations into the extent of the data compromise are expected to continue as authorities process the details of the digital intrusion.",
